ETL Option:


1.Checksum: 


Checksum is an initial and incremental loading technique which generates a Hash value which is of 4-byte number generated when an update or insert in the data table happens. In order to employee this technique your source table must have this function implemented on one of the columns that would generate the hash code. 

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Features of Checksum: 


Checksum is a system function
It cannot differentiate between upper case and lower-case values.
It is not able to generate hash values for NULL values.
It gives different values if the order of the data is changed even if the data is exactly the same.
The syntax of Checksum: Checksum (Expression) or Checksum (*)
Checksum supports all the datatypes except text, ntext, image, XML, etc.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Pro and Cons


Pro: 
Fast and easy to implement.
Good for Small to Medium Databases


Cons: 
Can Have Collisions.
Doesn’t Handle Some Data Types.
No Case Sensitivity.
Sensitive to Data Order.
