4.Time stamp


Introduction:
Timestamp is an incremental and initial loading technique that makes use of a datatype which is called as Timestamp. This datatype generates a unique binary number for each and every record in a table.
Whenever a record is inserted or updated a unique binary number is generated.
This binary number uses 8 bytes of storage space.
To recognize a Timestamp value a dataset must be having a datatype called Varbinary that is used to recognize the timestamp value.
Timestamp does not have any association with Date and Time.
To implement the incremental load and initial load with timestamp, we have to create a stored procedure.
